Turen APK/DEX Inspect is an original bounded, parse-only implementation of
Android binary XML (ResXMLTree), DEX, resources.arsc, and APK signing-block
parsing, informed by the publicly documented AOSP binary formats. No upstream
Android runtime code is included, and no Dalvik bytecode is ever executed or
emulated.

The compiled module links the following permissive Rust crates:
- zip 4.6.1 (MIT) — ZIP container reading; only the deflate read path via
  flate2's pure-Rust miniz_oxide backend is enabled.
- flate2 1.1.10 + miniz_oxide (MIT/Apache-2.0) — DEFLATE decompression.
- sha2 0.10.9 (MIT/Apache-2.0) — SHA-256 hashing of dex entries.
- serde / serde_json (MIT/Apache-2.0) — JSON output.
- wasm-bindgen 0.2.108 (MIT/Apache-2.0) — WASM bindings.

The compiled module also uses Rust standard-library components distributed
under Apache-2.0 or MIT. See Cargo.lock for the complete pinned dependency
closure.
